 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6088+) **The AI's final important-building retry now respects military-production pressure while another unit still fits its spending budget:** military-production logs showed that Base AdvCiv/K-Mod could reach the end of city production with strong reasons to build units, then give an important building one final chance that ignored that military pressure: in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseProduction`, short-circuit 2 already lowers building odds as `iBuildUnitProb` rises, but short-circuit 3 - the final "last chance to catch important buildings" immediately before generic unit production - recalculated its building chance from building value and land-war state alone. Strong military-production pressure could therefore survive the earlier production logic and then be partly forgotten at the final building retry. In the severe under-strength samples that exposed the issue, this late building retry won 7/9 and 7/8 times in two save-file 458 runs and 15/25 times in save file 457. To fix this, the AI now reduces only this final building chance in proportion to its existing willingness to build units, and only while the normal military-spending gate still has room; once the AI is already over that unit budget, the inherited building odds are left unchanged. The final save-file 458 validation left 375/640 already-over-budget evaluations untouched, while severe under-strength cases that still had spending room fell from about 48% average base building odds to about 33% and chose the building only 5/25 times. This keeps important infrastructure possible while preventing the last building retry from disproportionately overriding the military pressure already used by the surrounding production logic. See [KI#197.2](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#1972---fixedimproved-base-advcivk-mod-final-building-short-circuit-cvcityaiai_chooseproductions-short-circuit-3-ignored-buildunitprob-and-could-override-strong-military-production-pressure-immediately-before-generic-unit-production).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6089+) **Late floating-defender production now respects military-spending limits unless floating defenders are severely below need:** dedicated BBAI military-production logging exposed a Base AdvCiv/K-Mod inconsistency in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseProduction`: the earlier floating-defender pass checks unit spending before adding more defenders, but the later 50% retry did not. In the pre-fix save-file 457 run, 153 of 281 actual floating-defender-2 choices occurred at or above the normal `max+15` allowance, including 97 peaceful cases; save file 456 had 85 of 243 above the same threshold, including 70 peaceful cases. One extreme save-file 456 example had Persia only one floating defender short (6 available versus 7 wanted) while unit spending was already 220 against a normal maximum of 84, yet the late retry still produced another military unit. To fix this, ordinary peaceful shortages now require the normal `max+15` spending headroom, while land wars and severe floating-defender shortages may still use the retry; severe shortage uses the same threshold as the earlier floating-defender pass. In the final save-file 456 validation, 143 ordinary peaceful over-budget candidates were blocked and every actual over-budget choice was explained by the intended war/severe-shortage exceptions. Save file 457 independently reduced actual over-budget choices from 153/281 in the old run to only 12/233, all explained by 10 severe shortages and 2 land-war cases. See [KI#197.3](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#1973---fixedimproved-base-advcivk-mod-late-floating-defender-retry-ignored-military-unit-spending-limits-and-could-keep-producing-extra-defenders-far-above-budget-in-peace).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6089+) **Generic peaceful city-hunting-stack production now respects military-spending limits:** BBAI military-production logging exposed another Base AdvCiv/K-Mod spending bypass in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseProduction`: the generic "city hunting stack" heuristic can request `UNITAI_ATTACK` / `UNITAI_ATTACK_CITY` before the later generic military-spending gate, so it could keep growing an offensive stack even when the AI was already far over budget and not at war. In the pre-fix save-file 456 run, 9 of 53 actual `start city attack stack` choices occurred at or above `max+15`; only one was during a land war, leaving 8 peaceful over-budget stack starts. The clearest example was Roosevelt on turn 100: America had 3 cities, no land war and no immediate danger, unit spending 200 against a normal maximum of 76 (`max+15=91`), yet this branch still ordered another `UNITAI_ATTACK_CITY` Axeman. To fix this, generic city-hunting-stack production now requires the normal `max+15` spending headroom while at peace, while land-war behavior remains unrestricted; the separate bounded target-specific Barbarian-city attacker logic remains unchanged. In the final save-file 456 validation, 391 peaceful over-budget evaluations were blocked while 188 over-budget land-war evaluations remained eligible, and none of 44 actual generic stack starts were peaceful and over budget. Save file 457 independently blocked 351 peaceful over-budget evaluations while preserving 20 over-budget land-war evaluations; none of its 45 actual generic stack starts exceeded `max+15`. See [KI#197.5](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#1975---fixedimproved-base-advcivk-mod-generic-city-hunting-stack-production-ignored-military-unit-spending-limits-and-could-keep-growing-peaceful-offensive-stacks-far-above-budget).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6090+) **Naval-trade sea-explorer fallback now counts docked/queued ships and stops once the relevant water area is fully revealed:** BBAI military-production logging exposed an inherited Base AdvCiv/K-Mod edge case in the special naval-trade explorer branch. Its `<3` safety cap counted only units physically in the water area and it never required any unrevealed water, so it could ignore a substantial docked/queued navy and still build late `UNITAI_EXPLORE_SEA` ships after exploration was complete. In the pre-fix save-file 456 run, 25 of 32 actual choices occurred with zero unrevealed water and 22 of 32 occurred despite at least three actual sea-domain ships including docked/queued units; one turn-258 example had Germany build a 200-hammer Attack Submarine while the main ocean was fully revealed and three naval units were already docked. To fix this, the branch now counts actual sea-domain ships associated with the water area, including docked and queued ships, and requires at least one unrevealed water tile while preserving the inherited three-ship cap and 25% roll. In the confirming save-file 456 rerun, only 44 of 437 evaluations remained eligible and 8 actual choices were made; every one had unrevealed water and fewer than three corrected sea units, while three successful choices still had `seaExplorerTarget=0`, confirming that the distinct trade-exploration fallback remains active where useful. See [KI#197.6](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#1976---fixedimproved-base-advcivk-mod-naval-trade-sea-explorer-fallback-could-ignore-dockedqueued-ships-and-keep-producing-explorers-after-the-relevant-water-area-was-fully-revealed).
 - Rebalance perceived **iPower**: downweight some naval units; adjust certain land units (e.g., warrior, animals) to reduce **fake power** that triggers bad wars. See [Long_Comments/Long_Comments_XML.txt](/Long_Comments/Long_Comments_XML.txt) (search for `UnitAI notes (Units XML)`).
 - XML **DefaultUnitAI / UnitAIs / NotUnitAIs**: align roles with efficiency (e.g., swordsmen primarily offensive even if versatile; longbows defensive unless explicitly set otherwise).
 - Promotions logic in `CvUnitAI::AI_promotionValue`: add **hard rules** so AIs pick context-appropriate promotions (e.g., City Garrison for `UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE`, City Raider for `UNITAI_ATTACK_CITY`; avoid Woodsman/Medic on front-line attackers unless context justifies). Rules apply per **UnitAI** (not just by unit type); with exceptions like recon. See **[KI#47](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#47---fixed--addressed--enhanced-ai-choosing-poorly-promotions-for-its-units-now-added-a-set-of-hard-rules-in-which-case-some-promotions-are-not-good-and-to-ignore-as-is-most-efificient-in-most-times-and-rarely-cases-where-some-promotions-are-best-to-always-go-first-for-eg-as-of-no-city_garrison-first-for-unitai_city_defense-city_raider-first-for-unitai_attack_city-etc-if-any-more)**.

